{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing","id":1403000,"title":"Why is lightning an Air Elemental thing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-15T16:14:14-07:00","id":1403000,"title":"Why is lightning an Air Elemental thing?","content":"Now I think that there can be a good argument made that lightning is more a fire elemental thing. First of all there are the descriptions of the nature of fire as seen in elementals and in the dragon blooded. A bolt of lightning is a self-consuming moment of dynamic energy that exhausts itself. Bright, flashy, dramatic, only existing as it moves. What happens to something struck by lightning? They are left scorched, burned, or it will even start a fire. These are the qualities of fire traditionally. How does the game like to talk about the element of air? Subtle, all-around you, invisible, detached and even just flat out cold. Even other setting such Avatar the Last Airbender are willing to go with lightning being part of the scope of fire. So why is it with the air in the Exalted? Just because it is part of the sky? Should it even remain that way? This is more getting into the themes of the setting and the metaphysics but might be interesting to think about. What about you though? Are you fine with lightning being an air thing or did it never quite fit with you either?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T16:51:51-07:00","id":1403009,"title":"","content":"The Air Aspect isn't the lightning so much as the cloud it connects to, smiting the obstacles in its way from on high, thinking of its next move in terms of entire weather patterns, so many steps ahead that you will never catch it.<br /> <br /> The only thing that's ever bugged me about Exalted's elements are the color associations, blue-&gt;air, black-&gt;water, white-&gt;earth. It'd make a lot more sense to me with Blue-&gt;Water, Black-&gt;Earth, White-&gt;Air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T17:11:45-07:00","id":1403012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1403009#post1403009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Air Aspect isn't the lightning so much as the cloud it connects to, smiting the obstacles in its way from on high, thinking of its next move in terms of entire weather patterns, so many steps ahead that you will never catch it.<br /> <br /> The only thing that's ever bugged me about Exalted's elements are the color associations, blue-&gt;air, black-&gt;water, white-&gt;earth. It'd make a lot more sense to me with Blue-&gt;Water, Black-&gt;Earth, White-&gt;Air.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the color thing is because black is traditinally water in Chinese stuff. And maybe purposefully trying to avoid being Magic <i>too </i>much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T17:17:20-07:00","id":1403013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BogMod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing#post1403000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why is it with the air in the Exalted? Just because it is part of the sky?</div> </div> </div> </div>Storms have been the only identifiable encounter people have had with electricity for almost as long as there have been people. People saw lightning in the sky before they even manipulated fire.<br /> <br /> That carries deep mythological connotations. Has any culture ever had a god of thunder that was not strongly associated with the sky? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T19:08:34-07:00","id":1403031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1403013#post1403013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Storms have been the only identifiable encounter people have had with electricity for almost as long as there have been people. People saw lightning in the sky before they even manipulated fire.<br /> <br /> That carries deep mythological connotations. Has any culture ever had a god of thunder that was not strongly associated with the sky?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some metaphysical designations that split hairs about it in Daoism, via the Yijing. The trigrams for Thunder/Lightning (the two weren't really distinguished from each other here) and Wind are associated with the xing of Wood, because Wood is abstractly about new beginnings and action from nothing. Meanwhile, the trigram for Heaven is associated with the xing of Metal (the other Metal trigram being Lake/Marsh), though I am not as sure of the associations there.<br /> <br /> Going in a completely different direction, living by a mountain might skew perceptions a bit, especially if it's a volcano, as clouds of ash and dust can also produce lightning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T11:35:08-07:00","id":1403131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1403013#post1403013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Storms have been the only identifiable encounter people have had with electricity for almost as long as there have been people. People saw lightning in the sky before they even manipulated fire.<br /> <br /> That carries deep mythological connotations. Has any culture ever had a god of thunder that was not strongly associated with the sky?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably not. Going by classic mythology you often get into that double dipping on things with that kind of god. Thunder and lightning, storms, rain. No surprise weather played an important roll in many mythologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T17:44:39-07:00","id":1403163,"title":"","content":"Wikipedia, incidentally, has an index of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_thunder_gods\" target=\"_blank\">Thunder Deities</a>, so it's possible to just go down the list and pick out which ones weren't related to other details of the heavens. To begin, Sutekh seems to be one such example (he's closer to the desert, which fits my earlier hypothesis on the count of dust clouds).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T20:48:07-07:00","id":1403177,"title":"","content":"I mean the sea is only blue because it reflects the sky. Go down further and water is black. That's why black jade is Water-aligned. Black like the depths of the sea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T11:54:51-07:00","id":1403262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1403177#post1403177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the sea is only blue because it reflects the sky. Go down further and water is black. That's why black jade is Water-aligned. Black like the depths of the sea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wine-dark sea is something that's also confsuedf olks on Homer for like, ever as I gather. White yeah it is associated with blue, it being also assocaited with <i>darkness</i> in a way seems also pretty ancient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T10:53:37-07:00","id":1403401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1403012#post1403012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the color thing is because black is traditinally water in Chinese stuff. And maybe purposefully trying to avoid being Magic <i>too </i>much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both water and air would be blue in Magic, and earth would be red and maybe a little green, so I don't think the system is much less Magic-like than the alternative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T16:42:40-07:00","id":1403434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1403401#post1403401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both water and air would be blue in Magic, and earth would be red and maybe a little green, so I don't think the system is much less Magic-like than the alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now i'm thinking of Magic decks/worlds as peculiar almost-Creations amidst bordermarches, Wyld and beyond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T17:11:00-07:00","id":1403439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1403434#post1403434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And now i'm thinking of Magic decks/worlds as peculiar almost-Creations amidst bordermarches, Wyld and beyond.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Dragon-Blooded driven mad by the associations contained therein.<br /> <br /> &quot;They grouped lightning in with fire and earth! Why? How is it possible?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T18:23:15-07:00","id":1403450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1403439#post1403439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the Dragon-Blooded driven mad by the associations contained therein.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;They grouped lightning in with fire and earth! Why? How is it possible?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Damn, now i just remembered the Amabossar and 2e's take on them as a byproduct of a time after the Raksha Invasion when some elemental associations flowed and mixed in peculiar ways.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be outside Creation. And now i'm imagining a number of them in a spiritual quest to find &quot;the Sixth Pole&quot;, that one obscure place in Creation or the Bordermarches tainted in JUST the right way to make them whole once more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T12:33:33-07:00","id":1404960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1403009#post1403009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Air Aspect isn't the lightning so much as the cloud it connects to, smiting the obstacles in its way from on high, thinking of its next move in terms of entire weather patterns, so many steps ahead that you will never catch it.<br /> <br /> The only thing that's ever bugged me about Exalted's elements are the color associations, blue-&gt;air, black-&gt;water, white-&gt;earth. It'd make a lot more sense to me with Blue-&gt;Water, Black-&gt;Earth, White-&gt;Air.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's mainly this:<br /> <br /> -black is an odd color to associate with Earth, but the one color that makes sense (brown) is well...not very cool looking<br /> <br /> -Air is associated with blue because the sky is blue and and lightning bolts are commonly drawn blue<br /> <br /> -black is a bit of an odd thing for Water, but it makes more sense when you consider that the deepest places of the sea are near pitch black","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T13:06:41-07:00","id":1404965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1404960#post1404960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-black is an odd color to associate with Earth, but the one color that makes sense (brown) is well...not very cool looking</div> </div> </div> </div>Not terribly odd, all things considered. The Egyptian term for the land by the Nile where humans could live was Khem, the Black Land, in contrast to Deshret, the Red Land.<br /> <br /> The term Chernozem (in Exalted associated with Liminals) means the Black Earth and is an especially fertile sort of soil.<br /> <br /> Yin and Yang, Earth and Heaven, Black and White.<br /> <br /> Black being associated with earth is hardly uncommon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T13:44:04-07:00","id":1404970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1404960#post1404960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">black is an odd color to associate with Earth, but the one color that makes sense (brown) is well...not very cool looking</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you mean white here instead of black by any chance? Your post seems to be about explaining the color choices for Exalted, but Earth is white in Exalted, not black.<br /> <br /> I agree brown wouldn't be a great choice. Earth is also associated with yellow in Exalted, which I guess is the closest they could get to brown without losing all coolness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T14:07:17-07:00","id":1404975,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, sorry. I meant that.<br /> <br /> White makes a lot more sense, admittedly, when you remember that Earth in Exalted doesn't just literally mean dirt, but also stone such as marble and brilliant gems like diamonds. Basically, White Jade is supposed to be magic marble and porcelain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T14:29:42-07:00","id":1404976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1404975#post1404975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, White Jade is supposed to be magic marble and porcelain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that and actual white jade, which I think in some real life belief systems actually does connote some of the things attached to the Earth element. If nothing else, it is the rarest colour and thus the most valuable; it has often be made into treasures to be gifted to emperors.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T10:51:56-07:00","id":1409382,"title":"","content":"Especially in light of the mechanics for Aura, it would have been cool to see lightning treated as an intermediary between Fire and Lightning in the way many lava thematics get both fire and earth keywords. They could have done a similar thing with ice/snow as an intermediary of water and air. That would fix the other &quot;why is this air?&quot; question people ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T11:36:29-07:00","id":1409400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1404970#post1404970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you mean white here instead of black by any chance? Your post seems to be about explaining the color choices for Exalted, but Earth is white in Exalted, not black.<br /> <br /> I agree brown wouldn't be a great choice. Earth is also associated with yellow in Exalted, which I guess is the closest they could get to brown without losing all coolness.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, yellow is associated with \u201ccenter\u201d in some real world systems, and given the Pole of Earth is there, well. Going more Western, I would think yellow = gold. And the Immaculate Philosophy would prefer a common color to mean \u201cearth dragon\u201d rather than \u201csun god\u201d in the peasant mind.<br /> <br /> More curious to me is what is \u201ccolor of death\u201d in different parts of creation. If the jade color - element association is fairly universal, does that mean black = death in the West because of burial at sea? Blue is unlucky in the North?<br /> <br /> Course, then I start thinking Alchemy and wondering what the classical metals \u201cmean\u201d in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T12:49:22-07:00","id":1409610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpoonR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1403000-why-is-lightning-an-air-elemental-thing?p=1409400#post1409400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> More curious to me is what is \u201ccolor of death\u201d in different parts of creation. If the jade color - element association is fairly universal, does that mean black = death in the West because of burial at sea? Blue is unlucky in the North?</div> </div> </div> </div>If black is associated with death in the West, I'd suppose it would be because of the huge ancient shadowland more than anything.<br /> <br /> Still, the same culture can associate a colour with multiple things. There's a lot of volcanic soil over there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,